  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Friday)\nIssued at 1105 AM MDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nUpper level analysis depicts upper trof making its way onshore \ninto the PNW with broad ridging over the central US. The Northern \nPlains sits under southwest flow with water vapor imaging showing \na few weak waves and convection over the Rockies. High based \nstorms capable of damaging wind gusts and hail are possible over \nthe area this afternoon as modest CAPE develops over the region. \nThis morning's CAMs show some activity developing later this \nafternoon and evening.\n\nStronger wave/upper low moves in for Sunday from the PNW and \ngrazes the CWA. Modest CAPE will once again fuel high based \nconvection over the CWA Sunday afternoon. Again, the main hazards \nwith any storms that develop will be damaging wind gusts and hail.\nLow forecast confidence in storms developing as optimal forcing \nand moisture will be located to the north and west of the CWA. \n\nBroad ridging will continue over the central US with trof over \nthe western US. The CWA will sit under southwest flow, keeping \nconditions warm (highs in the 80s to 90s) with near daily chances \nfor afternoon storms to close out the month. There are some fire \nweather concerns for the end of this weekend into early next week,\nmainly over northeastern WY into far southwestern SD. More \ndetails in the fire weather discussion.",
